cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Hoist or its results, please cite the software and the paper."
title: "Hoist: an MCP proxy that reads ahead of your agent"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Nodeland
    given-names: Alex
repository-code: "https://github.com/alexnodeland/hoist"
url: "https://hoist.alexnodeland.com/"
license: MIT
abstract: "Hoist learns, from an LLM agent's recorded tool calls, which reads it makes next and where their arguments come from, and serves them through an MCP proxy in the same tool result, so the agent needs fewer LLM turns."
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-15
keywords:
  - LLM agents
  - Model Context Protocol
  - speculative execution
  - tool use
  - probabilistic programming
